               <history>
                  <origin>
                     <origDate when-custom="11XX" notBefore="1100" notAfter="1199"
                        calendar="#gregorian">s. xii</origDate>
                  </origin>
                  <provenance cert="low"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_36">Battle, Sussex.
                        Benedictine abbey of St Martin</orgName><p>Hereford, Cathedral, MS P. V. 1
                        and Bodleian, e Mus. 93, formed one volume, earlier probably at
                     Battle.</p></provenance>
                  <provenance><orgName role="fmo" key="org_66">Brecon, Brecknockshire. Benedictine
                        priory of St John the Evangelist</orgName><p>Later at the cell of Brecon.
                        Formerly contained also Gildas according to a note at the end of MS P. v. 1
                        in Sir John Prise's hand. Prise found it 'in Brechonia Demetarum . . . urbe
                        . . . ex coenobio Monachorum, quod ibidem erat Benedictini, quem vocant,
                        ordine desumptum' (Prise, <title>Historiae Brytanniae Defensio</title>,
                        1573, p. 114). See N. R. Ker, 'Sir John Prise', <title>The Library</title>,
                        5th ser. 10 (1955), 7.</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners"><persName role="fmo">Sir John
                        Prise</persName> (d. 1555).</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">e Mus. 93 belonged to <persName role="fmo"
                        >Silas Taylor</persName> in 1658, for whose dealings with Hereford library
                     see Wood, <title>Athenae</title>, 3. 1175. It formed part of the Hereford MS in
                     s. xvi (see Cambridge, CCC MS 101, pp. 132–133).</provenance>
               </history>
